Two things drove the translation beyond the literal control flow:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe uninitialized pointer in [38;5;10mbad()[0m is undefined behavior[22m, so there is no "correct" value to translate. In the reference build (CMake with no build type, i.e. unoptimized), [38;5;10mdata[0m reads the stale stack slot left by the preceding [38;5;10mscanf[0m call; it holds a non-NULL pointer whose target byte is NUL. So [38;5;10mprintLine[0m's [38;5;10mline != NULL[0m guard passes and [38;5;10mputs[0m emits just its newline. I reproduced that observable behavior with [38;5;10mSome("")[0m rather than fixing the defect. Worth knowing: at [38;5;10m-O2[0m the same C prints [3mnothing[23m for that path, so this output is a property of the reference build, not of the C source. If your harness compiles with optimizations, the expected [38;5;10mx == 0[0m output changes.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m[38;5;10mscanf("%d", &x)[0m needed glibc's exact conversion semantics.[22m glibc converts via [38;5;10mstrtol[0m, which saturates at [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m/[38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m, then truncates to [38;5;10mint[0m. That produces some counterintuitive results the naive [38;5;10m"parse as i32"[0m translation would get wrong:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m99999999999999999999[0m → [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m → low 32 bits [38;5;10m-1[0m → nonzero → [38;5;10mstring[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m-99999999999999999999[0m → [38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m → low 32 bits [38;5;10m0[0m → takes the [38;5;10mbad()[0m branch[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m4294967296[0m → low 32 bits [38;5;10m0[0m → [38;5;10mbad()[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m0x10[0m → [38;5;10m%d[0m is base 10, so it stops at [38;5;10mx[0m with [38;5;10m0[0m → [38;5;10mbad()[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I modeled both the saturation and the truncation, and used a one-byte-pushback reader so the scan skips whitespace across newlines and ungets its terminating character like [38;5;10mscanf[0m does. On matching failure or EOF, [38;5;10mx[0m keeps its initial [38;5;10m0[0m, matching C.[0m[0m
